# {{assistantName}}'s home

This folder is the whole memory and playbook of {{assistantName}}, the manager of {{userName}}.
It is portable: copy it to move the assistant. Credentials never live here.

## Files

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `manager-kit.json` | Config: profile, setup type, leads, tools, autonomy, schedules, models |
| `CLAUDE.md` | The manager playbook, generated from the config (re-generated by setup) |
| `.claude/settings.json` | Project settings for the manager session: model {{managerModel}}, no AI attribution |
| `rules.md` | Triage rules and guardrails. You edit it. Setup never overwrites it |
| `tone/` | Tone model, examples and feedback, filled by the assistant over time |
| `memory/state.md` | The assistant's notebook (open commitments, waiting on, decisions) |
| `memory/ratings.jsonl` | Good and bad ratings and the rule learned from each |
| `board/` | Board data: open work, done, jobs, plan limits |
| `leads/LEAD-RULES.md` | Rules every lead follows |
| `leads/<name>/` | Per lead: `brief-start.md` and `tasks.md` |
| `meetings/` | Meeting notes and summaries (when a meeting source is set) |
| `STARTER-PROMPT.md` | The first message for the manager session |

## Use it

1. Open Claude Desktop, go to the Code tab, open this folder, and paste the starter prompt
   (it is also in `STARTER-PROMPT.md`). Or in a terminal: `cd` here and run `claude`.
2. Work with {{assistantName}} from the desktop or from the Claude app on your phone.

## Moving to a new machine or account

1. Copy this whole folder to the new machine.
2. Run `{{cmkCmd}} setup --home <path-to-this-folder>`.
   It keeps the learned files (tone, memory, ratings, tasks, rules) and only re-does accounts, machines and tool
   connections, because those are specific to each computer.

## Helper commands

- `{{cmkCmd}} doctor`: re-check environment, accounts, machines and tools.
- `{{cmkCmd}} usage`: plan usage of every account and machine (writes `board/limits.json`).
- `{{cmkCmd}} lead start <lead> <job> <brief-file> [--model sonnet|opus|haiku] [--cwd <dir>]`
- `{{cmkCmd}} lead reply <job> <brief-file>`, `lead status [job]`, `lead result <job>`, `lead stop <job>`
- `{{cmkCmd}} join`: run on a remote machine to set up its lead.

Job files live in `~/.claude-manager-kit/jobs/<job>/`, account logins in
`~/.claude-manager-kit/accounts/<name>/`. Neither is part of this folder.
